// Freshness conditions on rules (Fernández and Gabbay, _Nominal rewriting_,
// I&C 2007; Pitts, _Nominal Sets_, CUP 2013). A rule between terms closes on
// a `where` clause, `where a # q`: the atom `a` stands outside the support of
// the term `q` stands for. A rule whose variable moves into or out of an
// abstraction states that atom fresh for it, or the description check refuses
// the rule for capture (`pathological/desc/freshness.gandr`). The value of
// `Theory` keeps each condition as a `Fresh` link after its rule. No port of
// these theories takes an atom, so no term names one: the support of every
// instance is empty and every condition holds. Where a port takes an atom, a
// condition decides where its rule fires:
// `model/desc/atom-occurrence.gandr`.

/// The π-calculus's structural congruence: the inert process, parallel
/// composition and restriction, scope extrusion moving `q` under the
/// restriction fresh for its atom. The checker orients the law and the kernel
/// replays the verdict.
theory Pi {
  sort Name : Atom;
  sort Proc : Type;
  oper nil : () --> Proc;
  oper par : (p : Proc, q : Proc) --> Proc;
  oper nu : (p : bind (a : Name). Proc) --> Proc;
  rule scope : par(nu(bind a. p), q) <=> nu(bind a. par(p, q)) where a # q;
}

/// Structural recursion over a rule chain: one per `Fresh` link, the
/// conditions its written rules state.
def rec conditions(chain : Theory) -> Integer {
  case chain {
    Rule(name, lhs, rhs, rest) => conditions[<](rest),
    Turned(name, lhs, rhs, rest) => conditions[<](rest),
    Fresh(atom, term, rest) => {
      run r <- conditions[<](rest);
      r + 1
    },
    _ => 0
  }
}

/// `Pi` states one condition.
@[ runs("1") ]
def stated() -> Integer { case Pi {
  Presents(sorts, opers, rules) => conditions(rules),
  _ => 0
} }
